<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/MIG_NACE2.1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#Correspondence"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/sections">
	<rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Level 1: 22 sections identified by alphabetical letters A to U</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/divisions">
	<rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Level 2: 87 divisions identified by two-digit numerical codes (01 to 99)</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/groups">
	<rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Level 3: 287 groups identified by three-digit numerical codes (01.1 to 99.0)</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/classes">
	<rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Level 4: 651 classes identified by four-digit numerical codes (01.11 to 99.00)</rdfs:comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0111/explanIncludes">
	<rdf:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;div&gt;
This class includes:&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
      Growing of cereals, e.g.:
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;wheat&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;grain maize&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;sorghum&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;barley&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;rye&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;oats&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;millet&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;
          pseudocereals, in other words, fruits or seeds used as cereals, e.g.:
          &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;quinoa&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;amaranth&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;chia&lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
      Growing of leguminous crops, e.g.:
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;beans&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;broad beans&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;chickpeas&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;cowpeas&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;lentils&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;lupines&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;peas&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;pigeon peas&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
      Growing of oil seeds, e.g.:
      &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;soya beans&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;groundnuts&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;castor beans&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;linseed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;mustard seed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;niger seed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;rapeseed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;safflower seed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;sesame seed&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;sunflower seed&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</rdf:value>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0111/explanExcludes">
	<rdf:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML">&lt;div&gt;
 This class excludes:&lt;br&gt;
  &lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;growing of rice, see &lt;a href="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0112" target="_blank"&gt;01.12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;growing of sweetcorn, see &lt;a href="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0113" target="_blank"&gt;01.13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;growing of maize, lupines or kale for fodder, see &lt;a href="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0119" target="_blank"&gt;01.19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;growing of oleaginous fruits, see &lt;a href="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/0126" target="_blank"&gt;01.26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/">
	<owl:imports rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos"/>
	<owl:imports rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/ux2/nace2.1/nace2.1">
	<owl:versionInfo>2.1</owl:versionInfo>
	<dct:description xml:lang="en">NACE Rev.2.1 is the classification of economic activities corresponding to ISIC Rev. 4 at European level. Though more disaggregated than ISIC Rev. 4, NACE Rev. 2.1 is completely in line with it and can thus be regarded as its European version. Since the national economic structures vary considerably, there are economic activities appearing in NACE Rev. 2.1 which are not of importance or do not occur in all Member States (e.g. categories referring to agriculture, mining and quarrying, manufacture of spacecraft, etc). The NACE Rev. 2.1 Regulation allows the Member States to use a national version derived from NACE Rev. 2.1 for national purposes. Such national versions must, however, fit into the structural and hierarchical framework laid down by NACE Rev. 2.1.</dct:description>
</rdf:Description>

